 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "harbourline-tower-tops-out",
   "title": "Harbourline Tower tops out at 28 storeys",
   "date": "2026-10-20T07:30:00",
   "categories": [
    "commercial",
    "company-news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "steel",
    "milestone"
   ],
   "featured_media": "tower",
   "excerpt": "The last beam went up on Friday, eleven days ahead of schedule. Here is what comes next on the harbour's newest office tower.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On Friday afternoon the final steel beam was lifted to the roof of Harbourline Tower, signed by every member of the crew. At 28 storeys and 112 metres, it is the tallest building our company has topped out, and we did it eleven days ahead of schedule.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How we gained the time</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"check-list\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list check-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Steel was pre-assembled into two-storey modules on the ground.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A second tower crane joined in month four for the core walls.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Concrete decks were poured at night during the summer heat.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Eleven days early on the structure means eleven days of float for the façade and fit-out teams. That's where projects usually slip.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Site superintendent, Harbourline</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What happens next</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The curtain wall is already on the lower twelve floors. Over the winter the building will be closed in, and interior fit-out starts in February. Tenants move in next autumn.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Thank you to the 340 people who have worked on site so far, and to our neighbours for their patience with the early-morning deliveries.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "sticky": true,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Lena F.",
     "email": "lena@example.com",
     "content": "Watched it go up from my office window every day. Congratulations to the crew!",
