  {
   "slug": "1000-days-without-lost-time",
   "title": "1,000 days without a lost-time incident at Northgate",
   "date": "2026-10-09T08:00:00",
   "categories": [
    "safety",
    "industrial"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "safety-culture"
   ],
   "featured_media": "hardhat",
   "excerpt": "Our Northgate crews passed a milestone this month. The superintendent explains the habits behind it.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This month our Northgate team passed 1,000 consecutive days without a lost-time incident. Across a site that has moved 80,000 cubic metres of earth and erected 4,200 tonnes of steel, that is a record we are genuinely proud of.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Three habits that made the difference</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Ten minutes every morning.</strong> The toolbox talk is never skipped, even on pour days.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Stop-work cards.</strong> Every worker carries one and uses it without fear.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Fix it today.</strong> Hazards reported in the morning are closed by the end of the shift.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>None of these ideas is new. What is different is that they are done every single day, by everyone, including the people in the site office.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The milestone belongs to the crew. My job was just to keep asking the question: what could hurt someone here today?</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Northgate superintendent</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "sticky": false,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Ana R.",
     "email": "ana@example.com",
     "content": "Proud to be part of this crew.",
     "date": "2026-10-10T06:45:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "millrace-crossing-opens",
   "title": "Millrace Crossing opens to traffic",
   "date": "2026-09-26T10:00:00",
   "categories": [
    "infrastructure"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "milestone",
    "bridges"
   ],
   "featured_media": "bridge",
   "excerpt": "The cable-stayed bridge opened three weeks early after two years of work over the river.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Millrace Crossing opened to traffic this week, three weeks ahead of the contract date. The 320-metre cable-stayed bridge replaces a 1960s crossing and adds a protected cycle lane and a wide footpath.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Project facts</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"spec-table\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-table spec-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Figure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main span</td><td>180 m</td></tr><tr><td>Stay cables</td><td>48</td></tr><tr><td>Concrete</td><td>21,000 m³</td></tr><tr><td>Steel</td><td>3,600 t</td></tr><tr><td>Peak workforce</td><td>190</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The towers were slip-formed in continuous pours, and the deck segments were cast on the riverbank and lifted into place, which kept most of the work out of the water during the fish migration season.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Keeping the work out of the water was the hardest constraint and the best decision we made.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Bridge project manager</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our thanks to the city's engineers, the river authority and the residents of the east bank.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "sticky": false,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "design-build-school-in-14-months",
   "title": "Designing and building a school in fourteen months",
   "date": "2026-09-12T09:00:00",
   "categories": [
    "commercial"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "design-build"
   ],
   "featured_media": "school",
   "excerpt": "How the design-build route let Westfield Primary open before the new school year.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When Westfield's old primary school failed its structural survey, the district had fourteen months to replace it before the new school year. A traditional design-bid-build process would have taken that long just to reach the start of construction.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why design-build worked</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"check-list\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list check-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>The architect, engineer and builder sat at one table from week one.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Steel was ordered while the interior layout was still being finalised.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>The district made decisions in weekly two-hour workshops, not monthly meetings.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:blueprint}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:blueprint}}\" alt=\"A blueprint floor plan\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:blueprint}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The first floor plan, sketched in week two and largely unchanged.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The school opened on schedule, under budget, with a gym that doubles as a community hall in the evenings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Design-build is not right for every project, but when time is the hardest constraint, it is usually the fastest honest route.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "sticky": false,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "post-tensioned-slabs-explained",
   "title": "Post-tensioned slabs, explained for owners",
   "date": "2026-08-30T08:15:00",
   "categories": [
    "industrial"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "concrete"
   ],
   "featured_media": "pour",
   "excerpt": "Thinner floors, longer spans and fewer columns. A plain-language guide to the technique we use in most parking structures.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Post-tensioned concrete sounds technical, but the idea is simple: steel tendons inside the slab are pulled tight after the concrete hardens, squeezing it so it can span further without cracking.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What owners gain</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Thinner slabs, which means lower building height or more floors.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Longer spans and fewer columns, which makes better parking layouts.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Less reinforcing steel overall.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What to watch</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Never core or drill a post-tensioned slab without scanning it first. Cutting a tendon is dangerous and expensive. We hand every owner a tendon map with the as-built drawings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>It's the most efficient floor we build, as long as everyone respects the cables inside it.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Structural engineer</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "sticky": false,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "apprentice-class-of-2026",
   "title": "Meet our apprentice class of 2026",
   "date": "2026-08-14T12:00:00",
   "categories": [
